**Yes.** In the additive <first-order structure>, the <quantifier-free formula>
$$
\boxed{x+x=x}
$$
holds exactly at zero, because cancellation in the additive <group> gives $x=0$. This <first-order formula> uses only the permitted <function> symbol and equality; it does not require a constant symbol for zero.

