= Solution
{parent=γ}

**No.** Definability of a <function> means definability of its graph. The same additive <structure automorphism> $s(x)=-x$ would have to preserve the graph of multiplication. It sends the graph point $(1,1,1)$ to $(-1,-1,-1)$, which is not a multiplication-graph point because $(-1)(-1)=1\ne-1$. This contradicts <automorphism invariance of parameter-free definability>.

