= Solution
{parent=β}

**Yes.** One is the unique identity element of multiplication, defined by
$$
\boxed{\forall y\,(x\cdot y=y).}
$$
The integer one satisfies the <first-order formula>, and testing at the actual integer one forces any satisfying $x$ to equal one. Thus this is a parameter-free <universal formula> even though the language has no named identity.

